<!--Serializer Documentation — EmitRules
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.documentation.EmitRules-->
<serdocumentation:EmitRules xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:sercap="org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.capability"
  xmlns:serdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.documentation"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Visibility, boolean, omit, QName/FQN, XSI (B14–B17, B21, B25)
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Visibility prefix emit (B14):
    private → localName "__" + name; protected → "_" + name; public → bare name.
    Visibility is SSOT; prefix is reconstructible. Same on composition instance attributes.
    
    Type-reference emit (B21):
    No BML-semantic prefixed xmlns (excluding xsi) → FQN-emit mode.
    Otherwise → QName-emit mode using namespaceBindings; first authored prefix wins.
    Missing binding in QName mode → BML_NAMESPACE_UNBOUND (no silent FQN fallback).
    xmlns:xsi alone does NOT force QName mode (B25 interaction).
    
    Boolean literals vs type refs (B15/B16):
    Boolean values → always lowercase true/false.
    Boolean.True/Boolean.False type refs → preserve as TypeExpression (QName or FQN per B21).
    
    Omit-by-default (B17):
    SHOULD omit: abstract/final/override/readOnly when false, empty containers, visibility
    when prefix encodes it, default-false flags, …
    Collection instance values: attribute-placed arrays emit JSON-like [ … ];
    element-placed arrays emit one tag per item (verbose form). Definition
    <value> stays a single payload (JSON list inside one value).
    
    MUST NOT omit: required identity, true flags, non-default enums, authoredPlacement (D9),
    authored CDATA form (D8), comments, member constraints / suggestions / groups (keep an
    element body — do not self-close aggregation or association tags that still have those
    children), …
    
    XSI infrastructure (B25):
    Re-emit every stored namespaceBindings entry (including xsi) and, when present,
    xsi:schemaLocation / xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation on root start-tag.
    Do not invent schemaLocation or xmlns:xsi when absent.
    
    Document root form (doc:DocumentFormat):
    SourceInfo.rootForm "block" (or omitted) → emit <block> and child <type>.
    SourceInfo.rootForm "type" → emit the type QName / TypeIdentifier as the root tag
    and omit child <type> and <name>. Nested definition wrappers follow BlockDefinition.wrapperForm:
    Sub-Blocks emit the unqualified name tag; embeds emit the type tag like the root.
    Legacy wrapperForm "block" (or omitted) stays <block>. Do not invent a child
    <type> on a legacy Sub-Block whose type was inferred as parentType.name.
    New documents from BomBuilder.create use rootForm type and omit xsi / schemaLocation.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="serdocumentation:XmlCommentsEmit" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="sercap:FqnToQName" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="sercap:VisibilityPrefix" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="doc:DocumentFormat" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</serdocumentation:EmitRules>
